WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.547
A deployment plan collects what you export from a site into one package.

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:09.803
In this video, we'll read how the All Features step is written, and

00:00:09.803 --> 00:00:12.252
what your own deployment step needs:

00:00:12.252 --> 00:00:15.400
a step, a source, an editor, and a registration.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.247
A deployment plan is an ordered list of steps.

00:00:23.247 --> 00:00:28.493
When you execute it, Orchard Core passes each step to every deployment source.

00:00:28.493 --> 00:00:34.300
The sources add recipe steps and files to a package, which contains a Recipe.json file.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:40.309
A deployment step of your own has three parts, which one registration ties together.

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:44.634
The step stores its settings in the plan, and the source adds recipe

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:46.796
steps and files to the package.

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:50.770
A display driver gives the step its card, summary, and editor.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.093
Let's read the All Features step.

00:00:57.093 --> 00:00:59.107
It derives from DeploymentStep.

00:00:59.107 --> 00:01:03.354
Name is saved with the plan, and the other properties hold its settings,

00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:06.130
here a single option, IgnoreDisabledFeatures.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.037
Category groups the step in the list of steps you can add to a plan.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:16.430
All Features uses Infrastructure, one of the CommonLocalizationSources that modules share.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:21.165
Title is the display name of the step, and the heading of its

00:01:21.165 --> 00:01:22.771
add and edit screens.

00:01:22.771 --> 00:01:29.730
A module declares its titles in an internal class of localization sources, such as FeaturesLocalizationSources.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.334
Mark Category and Title with JsonIgnore.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:38.112
A plan is saved as JSON, and these two values are never stored with it:

00:01:38.112 --> 00:01:41.400
they are always read from the type of the step.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:46.934
A plan stores each step under its full type name and its assembly name.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:50.723
The recipe step that creates plans uses the class name.

00:01:50.723 --> 00:01:55.880
If you rename or move the class, existing plans show the step as unavailable.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.428
A source implements IDeploymentSource.

00:02:02.428 --> 00:02:07.125
Deriving from DeploymentSourceBase checks the type of each step for you, and calls

00:02:07.125 --> 00:02:09.900
your ProcessAsync only for steps of your type.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:14.979
To add a recipe step, add a JSON object to the Steps of the result.

00:02:14.979 --> 00:02:19.843
The All Features source adds a Feature step that lists the enabled features,

00:02:19.843 --> 00:02:24.350
and the disabled ones too, unless Ignore disabled features is checked.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.296
To add a file, call SetFileAsync on the FileBuilder of the result, as

00:02:29.296 --> 00:02:31.198
the Custom File source does.

00:02:31.198 --> 00:02:36.290
Orchard Core creates sources with dependency injection, so a constructor can take the

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.080
services the source needs.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:47.255
A display driver derives from DisplayDriver of DeploymentStep and your step.

00:02:47.255 --> 00:02:52.170
DisplayAsync builds a Summary shape, which the plan shows for the step, and

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.660
a Thumbnail shape, which is the card in the list of available steps.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.607
Edit returns the editor shape, initialized from a view model.

00:03:01.607 --> 00:03:06.870
UpdateAsync binds the posted values to the step, and returns the editor again.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.946
To validate the input, add an error to the model state in UpdateAsync,

00:03:11.946 --> 00:03:14.962
as the Custom File step does for its File Name.

00:03:14.962 --> 00:03:18.320
The step is saved only when the model state is valid.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:24.028
Each shape is a Razor view in the Views folder of the module, usually under Items.

00:03:24.028 --> 00:03:28.140
The file name is the shape type, with dots in place of underscores.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.747
The edit view is the form.

00:03:30.747 --> 00:03:34.462
It binds an input to the view model with a tag helper, and

00:03:34.462 --> 00:03:38.990
uses the same wrapper and hint markup as the editors of the other steps.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:47.892
AddDeployment registers the source, the step, and the display driver together.

00:03:47.892 --> 00:03:52.090
The Features module calls it from its startup class for All Features.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.119
A module that works without Deployment, like Roles, calls it in a startup

00:03:57.119 --> 00:04:00.476
class marked RequireFeatures for OrchardCore.Deployment.

00:04:00.476 --> 00:04:04.430
The step is registered only when the Deployment feature is enabled.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:09.498
When the feature that registers a step is disabled, the plans that contain

00:04:09.498 --> 00:04:11.118
it keep the step's data.

00:04:11.118 --> 00:04:15.760
The plan shows the step as unavailable, with a Delete button and no Edit button.

00:04:20.027 --> 00:04:22.410
Let's use the All Features step.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:28.617
In Tools, Deployments, Plans, Add Deployment Plan asks for a name, and Create opens the plan.

00:04:29.499 --> 00:04:32.345
Add Step opens the Available Steps dialog.

00:04:32.345 --> 00:04:37.799
The steps are grouped by category, and the category of All Features is Infrastructure.

00:04:38.264 --> 00:04:41.221
Select Infrastructure to see the card of the step.

00:04:41.221 --> 00:04:44.864
It shows the title and the description from the thumbnail view.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.917
Add opens the editor.

00:04:46.917 --> 00:04:51.441
Its heading is the title of the step, and the checkbox, Ignore disabled

00:04:51.441 --> 00:04:53.850
features, comes from the edit view.

00:04:54.317 --> 00:04:57.881
Let's check Ignore disabled features, and select Create.

00:04:57.881 --> 00:05:02.307
The plan lists the step with its summary view, next to Edit and Delete.

00:05:02.759 --> 00:05:05.197
Execute lists the available targets.

00:05:05.197 --> 00:05:09.610
File Download builds the package from the steps of the plan, in order,

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.759
and downloads it as a zip file.

00:05:15.959 --> 00:05:20.677
In the package, Recipe.json lists the recipe steps of the plan in order.

00:05:20.677 --> 00:05:24.851
The one that the source added is the Feature step, and its name

00:05:24.851 --> 00:05:28.179
property selects the recipe step that imports it.

00:05:28.929 --> 00:05:35.683
On import, FeatureStep, the recipe step handler named Feature, enables and disables those features.

00:05:35.683 --> 00:05:39.029
A separate video covers writing a recipe step.

00:05:39.779 --> 00:05:45.820
To send the package somewhere other than a download, implement IDeploymentTargetProvider, and register it.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:49.757
Each target names the route of an action that sends it, and Execute

00:05:49.757 --> 00:05:52.239
lists the targets next to File Download.

00:05:54.239 --> 00:05:59.997
A deployment step is a step class, a source, a display driver, and a registration.

00:05:59.997 --> 00:06:01.699
Thanks for watching.

